buildSteps.detail:
S2 RISK/DATA, confirmed by reading the code: both syncs are insert-only and the pull re-adds or overwrites. (a) lib/sync/tombstones.ts: localStorage purify:sync:removed = [{table, kind, locator, at}]; push flushes them as supabase.from(table).delete().eq('kind', k).contains('locator', loc) and clears on success; pull skips any row whose canonical key has a tombstone newer than the row. (b) lib/bookmarks.ts: remove() and removeByLocator() write a tombstone for the 3 syncable kinds; new restore(b: Bookmark) re-inserts the same object (same id and addedAt) and drops its tombstone. The server delete waits until the undo window closes (UndoBar calls commit), so Undo never needs a server re-insert. (c) lib/bible/annotations.ts: every persist stamps `at` (ISO) on the value; export a plain writeVerseAnnotation(book, chapter, verse, value) and readVerseAnnotation for non-hook callers (Saved, the journal composer), sharing persist's empty check and event. (d) lib/sync/annotations.ts: push becomes update-then-insert per changed key (update ... .eq('kind').contains('locator') .select('id'); insert when 0 rows), driven by the purify:annotation event detail instead of a full insert-only sweep; a cleared annotation writes a tombstone and deletes; pull keeps the local value when local `at` >= row.updated_at, and never drops a local color when the row has none. Send `color` only after a one-time probe confirms the column (a PostgREST 'column does not exist' error must not fail the whole push). (e) SQL for the owner, run in the Supabase SQL editor before (d) ships; probe first with the anon-key curl (200/401/404/42703) per the probe rule:

```sql
-- 1. Highlight colours reach the server
alter table public.annotations add column if not exists color text;
alter table public.annotations drop constraint if exists annotations_color_check;
alter table public.annotations add constraint annotations_color_check
  check (color is null or color ~ '^[a-z]{1,16}$');

-- 2. The journal's own entries (step 4)
create table if not exists public.journal_entries (
  id uuid primary key,
  user_id uuid not null references auth.users on delete cascade,
  kind text not null check (kind in ('reflection', 'prayer', 'question')),
  body text not null default '' check (char_length(body) <= 20000),
  prompt text check (prompt is null or char_length(prompt) <= 500),
  source jsonb,
  created_at timestamptz not null default now(),
  updated_at timestamptz not null default now(),
  deleted_at timestamptz
);
create index if not exists journal_entries_user_updated_idx
  on public.journal_entries (user_id, updated_at desc);
alter table public.journal_entries enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "journal_entries_self_all" on public.journal_entries;
create policy "journal_entries_self_all" on public.journal_entries
  for all using (auth.uid() = user_id) with check (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

Tests in lib/sync/__tests__/pull.test.ts (same cappedApi idiom): a bookmark removed here does not come back on pull; an edited note is not overwritten by the older server copy; a highlight's colour survives a pull; the existing 1,500-row cases still pass.
